Q: Proc sql in data step A: <p>You can do this with the <a href="https://github.com/SASPAC/sqlinds" rel="nofollow noreferrer">sqlInDs</a> package from the <a href="https://github.com/yabwon/SAS_PACKAGES/tree/main" rel="nofollow noreferrer">SAS Packages Framework</a>:</p>
<pre><code>libname packages &quot;%sysfunc(getoption(work))&quot;;
filename spfinit url 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yabwon/SAS_PACKAGES/refs/heads/main/SPF/SPFinit.sas';

%include spfinit;
%installPackage(sqlInDs);
%loadPackage(sqlInDs);

data foo;
    set %sql(select * from sashelp.cars);
run;
</code></pre>
<p>Otherwise, you can use <code>proc ds2</code> instead and write FEDSQL directly in a set statement:</p>
<pre><code>proc ds2;
    data foo / overwrite=yes;
        method run();
            set {select * from libname.dataset};
        end;
    enddata;
    run;
quit;
</code></pre>
